    <!-- `.tcard .h` HAS NO STYLE HERE, AND THAT IS ADR-012 T1 (2026-08-09). It is 600 10.5px mono
         and `.sheet2 .ctx` below is 500 10.5px mono; ADR-009 D7 bundles the 400 and the 500 face,
         so the 600 resolved to the 500 and `Label.CardHead` was `Mono.Meta` under a second name.
         The rule is listed in android/gate/s22b_type_test.go's s22bUnimplementedRules, which
         resolves both weights through res/font/jetbrains_mono.xml and fails the day the two stop
         rendering identically. A bundled 600 face would be that day.

         AND SINCE 2026-08-09 THIS STYLE HAS A SECOND TWIN, DISCLOSED RATHER THAN MERGED. `Mono
         .Agent` below is `.prow .ag`, 600 mono, and the micro rung puts it at 10 sp beside this
         one - same size, same family, same tracking, and the same resolved face. It is NOT merged,
         and ADR-012 phase 2's P7 is why: that pair is identical only after a rung this app chose,
         while the design still draws the two rules at 10.5 and 10, so recording either as
         deliberately unimplemented would put a false statement about the design into the register
         that exists to hold true ones. -->
    <!-- origin: .sheet2 .ctx -->
